-**Sampling Formula:**
-The shader uses the following logic to sample values, assuming the origin is centered on the first voxel [S1, unofficial]:
-
-$$
-\text{volumeVoxel} = \frac{\text{position} - \text{volumeOrigin}}{\text{voxelSize}}
-$$
-
-$$
-\text{volumeUv} = \frac{\text{volumeVoxel} + 0.5}{\text{volumeResolution}}
-$$
-
-$$
-\text{uv0} = \text{volumeUvOffset0} + \frac{\text{volumeUv}}{\text{atlasResolution}}
-$$
-
-$$
-\text{uv1} = \text{volumeUvOffset1} + \frac{\text{volumeUv}}{\text{atlasResolution}}
-$$
-
-$$
-\text{value0} = \text{texture}(\text{volumeAtlas}, \text{uv0}).r
-$$
-
-$$
-\text{value1} = \text{texture}(\text{volumeAtlas}, \text{uv1}).r
-$$
-
-$$
-\text{return} \text{mix}(\text{value0}, \text{value1}, \text{volumeT})
-$$
+**Pseudocode:**
+```python
+def create_atlas_texture(volume_resolution, volume_origin, voxel_size, time_count, texture_filter, atlas_buffer, atlas_resolution, gl_context):
+    # Create texture object
+    texture = gl_context.create_texture_3d()
+    
+    # Set type and format
+    texture.set_type('HALF_FLOAT')
+    texture.set_format('RED')
+    
+    # Set dimensions
+    texture.set_dimensions(atlas_resolution.x, atlas_resolution.y, atlas_resolution.z)
+    
+    # Set data
+    texture.set_data(atlas_buffer)
+    
+    # Set filter
+    if texture_filter is None:
+        texture_filter = 'LINEAR'
+    texture.set_filter(texture_filter)
+    
+    # Upload to GPU
+    texture.upload()
+    
+    # Update uniforms
+    uniforms['volumeAtlas'] = texture
+    uniforms['atlasResolution'] = atlas_resolution
+    uniforms['volumeResolution'] = volume_resolution
+    uniforms['voxelSize'] = voxel_size
+    uniforms['timeCount'] = time_count
+    uniforms['volumeOrigin'] = volume_origin
+    
+    return texture
+```
 
 **Edge Cases:**
-- Precision: Uses half-precision (16-bit) storage, which may limit dynamic range compared to 32-bit floats [S1, unofficial].
-- Boundary: The sampling assumes the volume origin is centered on the first voxel [S1, unofficial].
+- If `timeCount` is 0, the atlas may be empty or invalid [S1, unofficial].
+- Precision loss occurs due to half-float storage [S1, unofficial].
 
